Make the NVM capability-store verification (NvmCapStores) a parameter of cheriot

Upstream hard-wires cheriot_tag_filter NvmCapStores(1'b1): a capability store to the NVM region
is turned into a read and compared with the NVM, never written. The CHERIoT RTOS SoC in
ibex/dv/cheriot-rtos-test-suite maps its writable code RAM (Sonata's HyperRAM, 0x4000_0000) as the
subsystem's NVM region to give it tags, and the cheriot-rtos loader stores capabilities into
import tables there, so boot would fail. This adds a top-level parameter NvmCapStores, default
1'b1 (upstream behaviour unchanged), which that SoC sets to 0. To be proposed upstream.

diff -ru a/hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/rtl/cheriot_mem_sys.sv b/hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/rtl/cheriot_mem_sys.sv
--- a/hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/rtl/cheriot_mem_sys.sv
+++ b/hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/rtl/cheriot_mem_sys.sv
@@ -20,7 +20,10 @@
   parameter addr_t                MetaSramBaseAddr = 'h1100_0000,
   parameter int unsigned          MemSizeRevbm     = 3072,
   parameter logic [NumAlerts-1:0] AlertAsyncOn     = {NumAlerts{1'b1}},
-  parameter int unsigned          AlertSkewCycles  = 1
+  parameter int unsigned          AlertSkewCycles  = 1,
+  // Capability stores to the NVM are verified against its contents (cheriot_wtrc), not written.
+  // 0 makes the NVM region an ordinary tagged memory, for SoCs that map writable RAM there.
+  parameter bit                   NvmCapStores     = 1'b1
 ) (
 
   input  logic clk_i,
@@ -250,7 +253,7 @@
     .NvmTopAddr(NvmTopAddr),
     .MetaMainSramTagBase(MetaMainSramTagBase),
     .MetaNvmTagBase(MetaNvmTagBase),
-    .NvmCapStores(1'b1)
+    .NvmCapStores(NvmCapStores)
   ) u_cheriot_tag_filter (
     .clk_i,
     .rst_ni,
